course: dictionary
lesson: 13849
title: Jocular: the friendly joke
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you the mood of a speaker. Read the words around the new word to find the clue. «Uncle Tom made a jocular remark about my messy hair, and we both laughed.» Uncle Tom is teasing, and he laughed too, so jocular must mean joking in a friendly way.
explain: Look at what happens next. «The teacher's jocular voice made the class giggle.» Nobody is upset, and the class giggles, so the voice was funny and playful. If a comment hurt someone's feelings, it would not be jocular.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning, «a funny remark», and check that the sentence still makes sense. It does, so your meaning is right.
fact: Jocular means joking, funny and playful in a friendly way.
fact: «Jocular» is a formal word, often found in stories and reports.
fact: A jocular remark is a joke or funny comment, not a serious or nasty one.
fact: The adverb «jocularly» means in a joking, friendly way: «"Careful," she said jocularly.»
exercise: «Grandad made a jocular remark about the rain.» What does jocular mean? | Very sad | Angry and loud | Cold and wet | *Joking and friendly
exercise: «Uncle Tom is a jocular man who loves telling silly jokes.» What kind of man is Uncle Tom? | A sleepy man who snores | *A funny, playful man who likes to joke | A serious man who never smiles | A loud man who shouts at people
exercise: Ellie says jocular means cross, because it sounds like a grumpy word. Is she right? | Yes, cross is the same | No, it means very quiet | *No, it means joking and friendly | No, it means very old
test: «The clown's jocular tricks made the crowd roar with laughter.» What does jocular mean here? | *Funny and playful | Tidy and neat | Frightening | Slow and sleepy
test: Which word is closest in meaning to jocular? | Angry | *Funny | Serious | Silent
exam: Which phrase best describes a jocular remark? | Rude and loud | *A friendly joke | Cruel and hurtful | Serious and secret
